---
MECHANISM (why 1–3 fail and 4 passes)
---

Three rails, still not equivalent (wave-1 still true on this ELF):

1. **Check / LLVM / emit-c front-door** (`check_secret_println_sinks`,
   HEAD / ELF): first `RPAREN` ends the walk.
2. **Stmt `println` belt** (`c_emit_print.oo` L19–30): per-arg IDENT
   scan also stops at first `COMMA` / `RPAREN` / `SEMI` (no depth),
   then `c_emit_expr_c` (depth-correct) + `oo_print_*`, then next arg.
3. **Free-call emit-guard** (`c_emit_lower.oo` L90 →
   `c_guard_scan_idents` on full C `args`). `eprintln` uses this.
   Stmt `println` never does.

`println((n), tok)` after sink `LPAREN`:
`LPAREN INT/IDENT RPAREN COMMA IDENT(tok) RPAREN`.
Front-door hits grouping `RPAREN` and never sees `tok` → check `OK`.
Stmt belt finishes first arg at that `RPAREN`, then the **next** arg
scan sees `tok` → emit-c SECRET after `oo_print_int((n));`.

`println((("x")+tok))` is **one** arg. Stmt IDENT scan:
`LPAREN LPAREN STRING RPAREN` → stop. Never looks at `tok`.
`c_emit_expr_c` then lowers the whole concat. Front-door same first-`)`
stop. emit-c **prints** `tok`. Check type-first on this ELF: arity
walker also steals the inner `RPAREN` → `println` looks like 0 args →
`ERR\ttype` “expects at least 1 argument”. **No secret walk.**

`eprintln(id(1), tok)`: check same first-`)` stop after `id(1)`.
emit-c is free-call → guard sees `tok` in joined args → SECRET.

`println(n, tok)`: no inner `RPAREN`. All rails see `tok`.

